I found several papers about language model agents that reason and use tools. The most cited one among them is "Toolformer: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Use Tools" by Timo Schick et al., published in 2023. It has 6294 citations according to Semantic Scholar.

Here is the BibTeX entry for that paper:

@article{schick2023toolformer,
  title={Toolformer: Language Models Can Teach Themselves to Use Tools},
  author={Timo Schick and Jane Dwivedi-Yu and Roberto Dessì and Roberta Raileanu and Maria Lomeli and Luke Zettlemoyer and Nicola Cancedda and Thomas Scialom},
  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:2302.04761},
  year={2023},
  url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04761}
}

The citation you used for "Generative Adversarial Networks" by Goodfellow is slightly incorrect in terms of the year. The correct year for the arXiv preprint is 2014, not 2016. Here is the correct BibTeX entry for the paper:

```bibtex
@article{goodfellow2014generative,
  title={Generative Adversarial Networks},
  author={Ian J. Goodfellow and Jean Pouget-Abadie and Mehdi Mirza and Bing Xu and David Warde-Farley and Sherjil Ozair and Aaron Courville and Yoshua Bengio},
  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:1406.2661},
  year={2014},
  url={https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.2661}
}
```

